{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>These are the generations of Noah</b> — four instances of juxtaposed אלה תולדות: אלה תולדות השמים, אלה תולדות נח, אלה תולדות שם, אלה תולדות יעקב. In all of them, what precedes is invalid (פסל): before אלה תולדות השמים — תהו ובהו is invalid; אלה תולדות נח — the generations before him are invalid; אלה תולדות שם — the children of Ham and the children of Japheth are invalid; אלה תולדות יעקב — Esau and his chieftains are invalid." "<b>Noah, Noah, etc.</b> — Three times נח is written in the verse: he saw three worlds. Another interpretation: he was of three, for each saved three by his merit: Noah saved his three sons, Shem, Ham, and Japheth; Daniel saved Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah through a dream; Job saved his three friends, Eliphaz the Temanite, Bildad the Shuhite, and Zophar the Naamathite. Another interpretation: Noah to the heavens, Noah to the creatures, Noah to those above, Noah to those below, Noah in this world, Noah in the world to come." "<b>He was wholehearted</b> — הי\"ה rises to the count of 20, to teach that he was wholehearted throughout all 20 generations from Adam to Abraham, but once Abraham came, he [Noah] was no longer counted as wholehearted." "<b>Noah walked with Elohim</b> — ס\"ת חכם (end-letters: samekh-tav of a word form חכם). As it is written: 'and takes souls — חכם.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:46.398855875Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}